    "title": "Utility crews work to restore power to 7,700 in Schenectady - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mike Goodwin ,\n11 hours ago National Grid crews on Wednesday worked to restore services to 7,700 customers who lost electricity on Schenectady's north side. (Tyler A. McNeil/Times Union) SCHENECTADY — National Grid is restoring service to more than 7,700 customers who lost electrical service Wednesday afternoon.\nService was restored to about half of the customers, company spokesman Patrick Stella said in a 1:20 p.m. email. He said utility crews hoped to have restoration complete within two hours.\nThe outage was caused by a problem in a substation along Rosa Road on the city's north side.\nSign up for Times Union newsletters here\nRead the original article on timesunion.com\n2",
